{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.68,"content_digest":"8d5ab0b23a317aab409a4e49e1f20c6db4b97d45fb7dd8778ddc45f9d27f415f","created_at":"2026-08-23T13:37:50+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"f49fe2f1a8ccccf756873a6183e1c0a5c81a7a1037a4dda89bb5c3ce10e46c36","input_tokens":5877,"latency_ms":34997,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"c3db54b24b98abc889c9947757133b6dea5bf007e89df54272ef2fef9e2dcd61","output_tokens":2487,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:18490969d0bf5c4655f82f3b","meta_principle_id":"meta:mathematics-logic:existence-construction-gap","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:scientific-discovery:01M0QDDYKT605M7JZZPCDPQ1SR","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The principle guarantees existence of a minimax-regret equilibrium in mixed strategies, but it does not assert that such an equilibrium can be efficiently constructed or computed. The meta-principle appropriately bounds the interpretation of the existence claim.","relation_type":"bounded_by","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T15:24:41+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0QKJMJD3A13DCG7YJ3ACW1G"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T13:37:50+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.9,"content_digest":"ec8fd9ad46913dbc0f6e8000f0bcbc52869c243b4e004489142017fe0e27eded","created_at":"2026-08-22T21:43:51+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"28391e9e7c72e2dde8452f38926e3c7594c0b647207080361a0f2c0b4fb64f6a","input_tokens":5726,"latency_ms":17415,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"b07b8a05ae55fb9278ad329c2e9d7608a797ee91d21241f17e4ad1e02657000f","output_tokens":2462,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:28b5aa3d79dde92367f0aa39","meta_principle_id":"meta:economics-game-theory:path-dependence-increasing-returns","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:ai-ml:01M0NPVNXX71GZERGN6ZH50QKC","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The meta-principle identifies switching costs and complementary assets as reinforcing mechanisms that can lock systems into path-dependent outcomes. The principle is a concrete instance: user-interaction data and legacy-service integration are reinforcing assets that increase switching costs and reduce user mobility between generative AI platforms.","relation_type":"supports","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T02:58:57+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0P5WC937PV7PKQMASBZ4D3Z"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-22T21:43:51+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.8,"content_digest":"6b0792976f554c33a44bacc1ef787ebf014d7a995a17d0896d78fa9f99409618","created_at":"2026-08-22T03:25:43+00:00","direction":"principle_to_meta","generation_trace":[],"link_id":"foundation-link:3a6f849ac2b9dd92d28fddfe","meta_principle_id":"meta:engineering-optimization:bellman-dynamic-programming","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:biology-medicine:01M0HGNXD5P8232QQRE7KB1VGF","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The polynomial-time dynamic programming solution for the relaxed augmented path problem at fixed λ is an application of the principle of optimality: the problem is decomposed into recursively optimal continuations, which is exactly the Bellman dynamic-programming structure.","relation_type":"depends_on","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-22T04:12:58+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0KTQZ6M68SKHPKARZR7EKFP"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-22T03:25:43+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.88,"content_digest":"4d525c3d3f0c8c2c6093139cdf30f24934bbdea506d76a36fea63fcc2b767ea1","created_at":"2026-08-22T16:09:01+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"da20e9fb2138e682fb27d086e9028cff4705f75bbdf4f502ca7974f25bbe788e","input_tokens":5581,"latency_ms":30906,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"9c2f27e5d9a20aeadc0ebaa92db6f858e57f238e81f697954e5750eb26201b27","output_tokens":2381,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:5e6b07c94af93eea7ce8d1b6","meta_principle_id":"meta:foundations:measurement-validity","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:neuroscience-cognition:01M0N3P5EVNDRJ8AJH9DVCF0X6","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The meta-principle states that a measured number is informative only if the measurement operation tracks the intended construct with adequate invariance across instruments, populations, or time. The principle reports that measured accessibility of the same report changes when the intended reader shifts from unaided human to machine, which is a concrete case of measurement dependence on the reader/instrument model. The finding is therefore consistent with the measurement-validity principle and falls within its scope.","relation_type":"consistent_with","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-22T17:07:53+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0N72WTZDNS3VF5QZJB70PZ5"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-22T16:09:01+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
{"condition_compatibility":"partial","confidence":0.55,"content_digest":"2c995082927de7034d2e0c2372b0298391c7f825eabaded6c230a844b793f7b3","created_at":"2026-08-23T13:12:30+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"209c1fa0eba4609abefd6f26e10a4d548583373273bfa561e3ce6dc41f20d5df","input_tokens":5627,"latency_ms":22537,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"94bce0933a33f0c2e1eaf868a7de8c833d98d11f6fbdbcc23aff1a9c756a892b","output_tokens":2531,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:bc0be2e2aef7593798240849","meta_principle_id":"meta:ai-ml:robustness-accuracy-tradeoff","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:ai-ml:01M0QBZXW8QGKTVXK83WTXQ3DR","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The meta-principle establishes that robustness to one class of perturbations can require features that do not serve other objectives, and explicitly notes that norm-bounded robustness may not correspond to semantic or physical perturbations. The principle's observation that adversarial training improves adversarial robustness but not occlusion/natural-corruption robustness is consistent with this trade-off framing, though the meta-principle's primary outcome is standard accuracy rather than natural-corruption robustness.","relation_type":"consistent_with","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T15:24:41+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0QKJMJD3A13DCG7YJ3ACW1G"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"compatible","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-23T13:12:30+00:00","variable_compatibility":"partial"}
{"condition_compatibility":"compatible","confidence":0.72,"content_digest":"6e79abb26523711361c608b6920b56d04f417c020adc2c404db246ac13d24af9","created_at":"2026-08-22T20:44:07+00:00","direction":"meta_to_principle","generation_trace":[{"attempts":1,"input_sha256":"85590a9b748af7dd926c9f0379645ee0fe6868a57a7859f84af8407fcad94ba9","input_tokens":5692,"latency_ms":22058,"model":"deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash","output_sha256":"e33c24400833c48ba63a3829a16f6e7ac01ff07f46cc8662f258d908f1ab520f","output_tokens":2421,"prompt_sha256":"a0e24249a3438877119c33b7ce1b688152e1189df5765ebd53fae91f7c321069","prompt_template":"meta-grounding-v1","provider":"siliconflow","repair_attempted":false,"schema_valid":true,"transport_attempts":1}],"link_id":"foundation-link:f1e154826ef6ae94b3148b26","meta_principle_id":"meta:engineering-optimization:human-factors","meta_principle_revision":1,"principle_id":"prn:ai-ml:01M0NKE5CF5A22CAXN8JDSDEJG","principle_revision":1,"rationale":"The finding that users rely on human fallback when explainability evidence is insufficient exemplifies the human-factors principle that operator behavior is part of the joint cognitive-technical system. The meta-principle frames such reliance as an adaptive system response rather than an external failure, which matches the claim's boundary condition that explainability outputs alone are inadequate for blind and low-vision users.","relation_type":"consistent_with","review_attestation":{"actor":"principia-owner","basis":"Explicit Submit reviewed changeset confirmation in local Admin","reviewed_at":"2026-08-23T02:58:57+00:00","source_review_status":"unassessed","trace_id":"sync:01M0P5WC937PV7PKQMASBZ4D3Z"},"review_status":"reviewed","revision":1,"scale_compatibility":"partial","schema_version":"global-foundation-link-v1","status":"active","updated_at":"2026-08-22T20:44:07+00:00","variable_compatibility":"compatible"}
